-- title:
--   Annulus at a node from an oriented étale crossing chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $p \mid M$, $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit that reduces to $1$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$, and $hj$ asserting that `jqModC ℚ` lies in the level-$SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$ $q$-expansion function field; let $\mathfrak{X} :$ `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` be a Deligne–Rapoport model package for $\Gamma_H(M)$ at $p$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, residue field algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and $\rho : R_p \to A$ compatible with $R_p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with $\rho_O : R_p \to O$, maximal ideal $(p)$, a surjection $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa_A$ with $\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O = \mathrm{res} \circ \rho$, a map $j_O : O \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $R_p$, and $\iota_A : O \to A$ with $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ after $\iota_A$ equal to $j_O$ and residue equal to $\mathrm{to}\kappa$. Let $n$ be a point of the pullback of the two morphisms `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` and `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 1` furnished by $\mathfrak{X}$, and let $x_n$ be its image in $X_O =$ `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO` along the first projection, the component map of index $0$ and `bcMap`. Let $e \ge 1$, let $U$ be an open of $X_O$ containing $x_n$, and let $f : U \to \operatorname{Spec} O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1 - p^e)$ be a morphism over $\operatorname{Spec} O$ such that: the two coordinates $U, V$ both vanish at $y \in U$ exactly when $y$ maps to $x_n$; at every point over $x_n$ the stalk map of $f$ is flat, carries the maximal ideal onto the maximal ideal and induces an isomorphism of residue fields, and $f$ is étale on some neighbourhood; and, for the orientation, $V$ vanishes at $y$ iff $y$ lies in the image of the index-$0$ component map composed with `bcMap`, while $U$ vanishes at $y$ iff $y$ lies in the image of the index-$1$ one. Write $X_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}$ for the base change of `toBase p (ΓM M H) hj` to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $\mathrm{pr}_J : X_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}} \to X_O$ for the map induced by $j_O$, and $g_v, g_u \in \Gamma(X_O, U)$ for the pullbacks along $f$ of the coordinates $V$ and $U$. The conclusion is that the generic point of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C$ lies in the preimage of $U$ under $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}_J$, so that reading sections along $\mathrm{pr}_J$, $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$, the germ at that generic point and $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$ gives a ring map $\mathrm{read} : \Gamma(X_O,U) \to \overline{F}_{M,H} =$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H`, and that there exists an annulus `An` of $\overline{F}_{M,H}$ along $A$ — that is, a set `An.dom` of places of $\overline{F}_{M,H}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (valuation subrings containing $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, proper, principal), a parameter `An.param`, and a modulus `An.modulus` in the maximal ideal of $A$, subject to the annulus axioms: every place of the domain is rational and assigns the parameter a non-zero value in $\mathfrak{m}_A$ dividing the modulus, every such admissible value is attained by exactly one place of the domain, $\mathrm{param} - P(\mathrm{param})$ has order $1$ at each $P$ in the domain, and the unit principle holds — such that: a place $W$ lies in `An.dom` precisely when $W$ is rational (the residue field of $W$ is generated by $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) and there is a section $s : \operatorname{Spec} A \to U$ over $\operatorname{Spec} O$ via $\iota_A$ whose composite with $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \hookleftarrow A$ is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point attached to $W$ by $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}^{-1}$ followed by $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$ and $\mathrm{pr}_J$, and whose closed point maps to $x_n$; moreover `An.param` $= \mathrm{read}(g_v)$ and `An.modulus` $= \iota_A(p^e)$; and finally the generic point of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Mfib}\,A\,hA\,\rho\,h\rho$ lies in the preimages of $U$ under the two composites of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{efib}$ with the index-$1$ and index-$0$ component maps and `bcMap`, and the place `𝔛.placeOn1 A hA ρ hρ n` has order $1$ at the function-field element obtained by reading $g_v$ through the index-$1$ composite, while `𝔛.placeOn0 A hA ρ hρ n` has order $1$ at the element obtained by reading $g_u$ through the index-$0$ composite.
--
--   This is the construction of the annulus (the formal fibre, or tube, of a node) attached to a crossing point of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$ at $p$, extracted from an oriented étale chart $xy = p^e$ on the model over $O$: the domain of the annulus is described by the $A$-sections through the node, its parameter is the reading of one chart coordinate in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\cdot F(\Gamma_H(M))$, its modulus is $p^e$, and the two coordinates restrict to uniformisers at the node on the two components of the special fibre. It feeds the statement [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_width_annulus_attachedBothEnds_of_jHPlaceSpecialization_of_offDiag`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_width_annulus_attachedBothEnds_of_jHPlaceSpecialization_of_offDiag), where the widths of these annuli enter the semistable-reduction analysis.
